TEXT 0 800 Left 2 ;WHAT CHANGED IN THIS FILE, AND WHY\nSame driver as the closed and open files. (The driver is the Scan-Speak 26W/8534G00, not SEAS.) Cab = 0.621u is the real 88 L box.\nMab: was a 0 H inductor with Rser=1p -> NOW a plain wire. LTspice gives wrong answers with that combination (vented peaks came out 13 and 15 ohm instead of 31 and 50).\nMmd: was 39.94 g -> NOW 36.19 g. The 39.94 g from the free-air measurement already includes the air on the cone, and Ma1f (3.75 g) adds that air again.\n      So Mmd = 39.94 g - 3.75 g, and the total stays 39.94 g.\nCms: NOW 1.229 mm/N in every file. This is the rubber suspension of the driver only, from extract_ltspice.m. The driver is the same in all three boxes, so these values never change.\nMap: NOW {1.2*Lvent/3.318m}, which is rho*L/S of the tube. Ma1p: NOW 17.3, the air at the tube ends. Lvent is stepped over the three lengths we measured, so one run gives all three curves.\nnf_Cone, nf_Vent: NEW outputs. Near-field pressure p = s*rho*U/(pi*a), in Pa per volt, to compare with labD_nf_cone_L* and labD_nf_vent_L*. Read them as magnitude.\nRESULT, low peak / dip / high peak, simulated (measured in brackets), to see it plot 1/I(Vd1):\n160 mm: 11.3 (12.0) / 23.4 (23.4) / 46.7 (45.5) Hz.   200 mm: 10.6 (11.2) / 21.6 (22.8) / 45.9 (44.9) Hz.   240 mm: 9.9 (10.9) / 20.3 (21.5) / 45.3 (44.2) Hz.\nThe dip moves 3.1 Hz from 160 to 240 mm, the measurement only 1.9 Hz, so the real vent does not follow rho*L/S exactly. Write that in the report.
